      "description": "Cockroach Janata Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke on Tuesday thanked the organisers of a Ramlila event in Delhi for what he called \"free publicity\" after they announced plans to burn a 30-foot cockroach effigy alongside those of Ravan, Meghnad and Kumbhkaran.\n\"Thank you for the free publicity,\" Dipke said in reaction to the development.\nCJP legal head Ratna Singh also reacted to the controversy, describing it as a \"tamasha\" (drama).\nThe Shree Keshav Ram Leela Committee, which organises the annual event in Pitampura, has said the cockroach effigy is intended to symbolise filth and dirt and promote cleanliness under the Swachh Bharat and Swachh Delhi campaigns.\nCommittee president and BJP MLA Ashok Goel has maintained that the decision was not politically motivated and was intended to convey the message of the victory of good over evil while highlighting the importance of cleanliness.\nThe development comes amid protests by the CJP in the national capital. The group initially prote",
